# Scancodes 656..659 mapped to MACRO_1..4 in stock's file and here until
# session 16. Dropped for two independent reasons: MACRO keys are swallowed by
# PhoneWindowManager before any user-configurable layer can see them (see the
# header), and this folio was never observed to emit 656/657 — stock reaches
# APP1/APP2 through the HID usages 0x0c0398/0x0c0399 below, which is the form
# the kernel actually produces for a HID-over-UART consumer page.
#
# ⚠️ If `getevent -lt` on the folio ever shows scancode 656/657 instead of
# MSC_SCAN 000c0398/000c0399, add `key 656 F19` / `key 657 F20` here — stock
# maps BOTH forms, and mapping both is harmless because they resolve to the
# same keycode.

# Keys defined by HID usages
key usage 0x0c0067 WINDOW
key usage 0x0c006F BRIGHTNESS_UP
key usage 0x0c0070 BRIGHTNESS_DOWN
key usage 0x0c0079 KEYBOARD_BACKLIGHT_UP
key usage 0x0c007A KEYBOARD_BACKLIGHT_DOWN
key usage 0x0c007C KEYBOARD_BACKLIGHT_TOGGLE
key usage 0x0c0173 MEDIA_AUDIO_TRACK
key usage 0x0c019C PROFILE_SWITCH
key usage 0x0c01A2 ALL_APPS
key usage 0x0d0044 STYLUS_BUTTON_PRIMARY
key usage 0x0d005a STYLUS_BUTTON_SECONDARY

# Lenovo lapis custom key
key usage 0x0c038e LOCK
key usage 0x0c0391 MUTE
# F7, printed as the touchpad on/off key. Routed to a spare F-key so it is
# assignable, but with NO default action, because "turn the touchpad off" cannot
# be done properly on this build. Both routes were implemented and tested:
#
#   InputSettings.setTouchpadsEnabled  -> silently does nothing. It is gated on
#       isTouchpadDisableFeatureFlagEnabled() (InputSettings.java:440,:644) and
#       the aconfig flag com.android.hardware.input.touchpad_disable is absent
#       here (`adb shell aflags list | grep touchpad_disable` returns nothing),
#       so useTouchpads() short-circuits to true. The write appears to succeed.
#
#   InputManager.disableInputDevice    -> works, and was verified to affect only
#       the folio touchpad (17ef:62b2, SOURCE_TOUCHPAD, external) and never the
#       panel or the digitiser, which are 0000:0000 internal devices. But
#       re-enabling was unreliable in the owner's hands.
#
# ⚠️ The second route also used to be rejected because "it drops the tablet out
# of desktop mode: ShellDesktopMode gates on hasAnyTouchpadDevice, so turning the
# touchpad off closes every desktop window". THAT REASON IS NOW VOID -- session
# 19 turned desktop windowing off outright
# (overlay/FrameworkOverlayMalbec/res/values/config.xml:
# config_isDesktopModeSupported and config_canInternalDisplayHostDesktops, both
# false), so there are no desktop windows to close.
#
# The outcome is unchanged anyway, for a reason that outranks both: the owner
# ruled in session 19 that there should be no touchpad-toggle key -- it had been
# tried and was not useful. Recorded rather than deleted so the next reader does
# not resurrect the feature on the grounds that the stated obstacle disappeared.
#
# So the mapping stays (the key is worth something) and the action does not.
# ⚠️ Until session 17 this usage was not in this file at all, so the key reached
# the framework as KEY_UNKNOWN and did nothing at all. Owner-measured with
# work/scripts/60-keyboard-key-probe.sh.
key usage 0x0c0392 F17
# Fn + right-hand key 1. Stock calls it GLOBAL_SEARCH. KEYCODE_SEARCH is not
# usable here: KeyGestureController.java:1082-1090 only acts on it when
# config_searchKeyBehavior == 1 (TARGET_ACTIVITY), and AOSP's default is 0, so
# the key falls through and nothing handles it. Bound through our own picker
# instead, defaulting to LAUNCH_SEARCH.
key usage 0x0c0393 F23
# F9, printed "Full screen". ⚠️ It used to map to KEYCODE_FULLSCREEN and was
# DEAD, for a chain that is invisible from here:
#
#   KeyGestureController.java:871-882 turns KEYCODE_FULLSCREEN into
#   KEY_GESTURE_TYPE_TOGGLE_FULLSCREEN (82) rather than MULTI_WINDOW_NAVIGATION
#   (53), because toggle_fullscreen_state_via_fullscreen_key is ENABLED
#   READ_ONLY in bp4a — verified in
#   build/release/aconfig/bp4a/com.android.window.flags/.
#
#   Gesture 82 has exactly one registrar in the whole tree:
#   DesktopModeKeyGestureHandler.kt:62-77, and WMShellModule.java:1269 only
#   constructs it when desktopState.canEnterDesktopMode(). This device sets
#   config_isDesktopModeSupported=false and config_canInternalDisplayHostDesktops
#   =false (overlay/FrameworkOverlayMalbec), which is a deliberate, owner-accepted
#   decision — so 82 is never registered and handleKeyGesture drops it silently.
#
# So the key printed "Full screen" did nothing at all. F24 was the one unassigned
# F-key left (pen holds F13-F16 and F18; this folio holds F17, F19-F23), so the
# key now goes through MalbecParts' picker like every other ZUI key with no AOSP
# equivalent — the same treatment 0x0c0395 and 0x0c0397 already get.
key usage 0x0c0394 F24
# F10, the split-screen key. It used to map to RECENT_APPS, which is why it
# opened the recents list instead of splitting the screen — owner-reported, and
# visible in dumpsys input's last-handled gestures (keycode 312 ->
# KEY_GESTURE_TYPE_RECENT_APPS). AOSP has the action but only as a gesture
# (SPLIT_SCREEN_NAVIGATION_LEFT/RIGHT, 27/28, both in this unit's
# mSupportedKeyGestures), never as a keycode, so it goes through the picker.
key usage 0x0c0395 F21
# F11, printed as PC/phone link. That feature is ZUI's and has no AOSP
# equivalent, so rather than leave a dead key it becomes assignable with no
# default.
key usage 0x0c0397 F22
# The two keys to the right of F12. Owner-measured with
# work/scripts/60-keyboard-key-probe.sh: the AI/search key sends 0x0398 on its
# own and 0x0393 with Fn; the apps/settings key sends 0x0399 on its own and
# 0x039b with Fn. Stock's capability table for 17ef:62b2 calls the plain presses
# support_diy_app1 / support_diy_app2 — they are meant to be user-assigned,
# which is why they appeared to "do nothing".
# F19/F20 rather than MACRO_1/MACRO_2 — see the header for why MACRO is
# structurally unbindable on this ROM.
key usage 0x0c0398 F19
key usage 0x0c0399 F20
key usage 0x0c039b SETTINGS
# Cover closed / opened. Stock names these KEYBOARD_RESTORE / KEYBOARD_REVERSE.
# See the header for the measurement: 655 is the only half that can ever work,
# and configs/device_state_configuration.xml carries the other half.
key 654   WAKEUP    WAKE
key 655   SLEEP

# Joystick and game controller axes.
# Axes that are not mapped will be assigned generic axis numbers by the input subsystem.
axis 0x00 X
axis 0x01 Y
axis 0x02 Z
axis 0x03 RX
